2. सु (= √ 1. सू) cl. 1. 2. P. (Dhātup. xxii, 43 and xxiv, 32; सवति, सौति, only in 3. sg. pr. सौति and 2. sg. Impv. सुहि)
to urge, impel, incite, ŚBr.; KātyŚr.;
to possess supremacy, Dhātup.

3. सु cl. 5. P. Ā. (Dhātup. xxvii, 1) सुनो॑ति, सुनुते
(in RV. 3. pl. सुन्व॑न्ति, सुन्विरे॑ [with pass. sense] and सुष्वति;
p. सुन्व॑त् or सुन्वान॑ [the latter with act. and pass. sense] ib.;
pf. सुषाव, सुषुम &c., ib.; MBh.;
p. in Veda सुषुव॑स् and सुष्वाण॑ [the later generally with pass. sense; accord. to Kāś. on Pāṇ. iii, 2, 106, also सुषुवाण with act. sense];
aor. accord. to Gr. असावीत् or असौषीत्, असोष्ट or असविष्ट;
in RV. also Impv. सो॑तु, सुत॑म्, and p. [mostly pass.] सुवान॑ [but the spoken form is स्वान॑ and so written in SV., सुव्˚ in RV.];
and 3. pl. असुषवुः, AitBr.;
fut. सोता, ib.;
सोष्यति, KātyŚr.;
सविष्यति, ŚBr.;
inf. सो॑तवे, सो॑तोस्, RV. : Br.;
सोतुम् Gr.;
ind.p. -सु॑त्य, Br.;
-सूय, MBh.),
to press out, extract (esp. the juice from the Soma plant for libations), RV.; AV.; ŚBr.; KātyŚr.; Up.; MBh.;
to distil, prepare (wine, spirits &c.) Sch. on Pāṇ. ii, 2, 132 :
Pass. सूय॑ते (in RV. also Ā. 3. sg. सुन्वे and 3. pl. सुन्विरे॑ with pass. sense; aor. अ॑सावि, ib.) :
Caus. -सावयति or -षावयति (see अभि-षु and प्र-√ सु; aor. असूषवत्, accord. to some असीषवत्) Gr.:
Desid. of Caus. सुषावयिषति, ib. :
Desid. सुसूषति, ˚ते, ib. :
Intens. सोषूयते, सोषवीति, सोषोति, ib.

5. सु॑ ind. (opp. to दुस् and corresponding in sense to Gk. εὖ;
perhaps connected with 1. व॑सु, and, accord. to some, with pron. base स, as कु with क;
in Veda also सू॑ and liable to become षु or षू and to lengthen a preceding vowel, while a following न may become ण;
it may be used as an adj. or adv.), good, excellent, right, virtuous, beautiful, easy, well, rightly, much, greatly, very, any, easily, willingly, quickly (in older language often with other particles;
esp. with उ, = ‘forthwith, immediately’;
with मो i.e. मा उ, = ‘never, by no means’ ;
सु॑ कम् often emphatically with an Impv., e.g. ति॑ष्ठा सु॑ कम् मघवन् मा॑ परा गाः, ‘do tarry O Maghavan, go not past’, RV. iii, 53, 2;
सु always qualifies the meaning of a verb and is never used independently at the beginning of a verse;
in later language it is rarely a separate word, but is mostly prefixed to substantives, adjectives, adverbs and participles, exceptionally also to an ind.p., e.g. सु-बद्ध्वा, ‘having well bound’, Mṛcch. x, 50;
or even to a finite verb, e.g. सु-निर्ववौ, Śiś. vi, 58), RV. &c.;

1. सू (not separable in all forms fr. √ 2. सू; cf. 1. सु-षू॑, असु-सू, and √ 4. सु) cl. 6. P. (Dhātup. xxviii, 115) सुव॑ति (in Br. also ˚ते, and accord. to Dhātup. xxii, 43 and xxiv, 32 also सवति and -सौति; pf. सुषुवे॑, AV.; p. सुषुवाण॑, q.v.; aor. असावीत्, साविषत्, RV. :
Pass. सूय॑ते, Br. &c.), to set in motion, urge, impel, vivify, create, produce, RV. &c. &c.;
to hurl upon, Bhaṭṭ.;
to grant, bestow (esp. said of Savitṛ), RV.;
to appoint or consecrate to (Ā. ‘to let one's self be consecrated’), AV.; TS.;
to allow, authorize, ŚBr. :
Intens. सोषवीति, to urge or impel violently (said of Savitṛ), RV.

